# Scratch space for local test/demo runs (e.g. short STN logger validation
# runs) -- never meant to be committed, kept out of /tmp so it's easy to
# find in a file manager instead of buried in the OS temp dir. Local-only,
# not tracked at all (not even as an empty dir).
/tmp_demo/

# Compiled binaries (make/make rebuild in source_code/meta_heuristics)
source_code/meta_heuristics/moead
source_code/meta_heuristics/nsga2

# wflop_instances/ (Cazzaro/Pisinger "New Sites" real-world instance set,
# ~700MB, 501 instances) is intentionally NOT ignored -- committed in
# full, since git is the transfer path to the supercomputer, and
# hand-picking a subset now would just mean repeating this dance again
# whenever more of these 500+ instances are needed later.
#
# instances/site/ns<id> are symlinks into it, created on demand by
# run_one.sh the first time a given instance is actually used -- not
# committed themselves (they're machine-specific relative symlinks,
# regenerated automatically wherever wflop_instances/ exists).
instances/site/ns*
